From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] Offer Xlib surfaces for X11 windows

VK_KHR_xlib_surface is advertised as a guest-provided instance extension, so
Xlib clients (Wine and Proton through DXVK and VKD3D, SDL) can create the same
virtual X11-window surface as XCB clients; caboose-wsi/mesa_surface.inc binds
it to the window and never uses the Display.
---
 src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan/gfxstream_vk_device.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan/gfxstream_vk_device.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan/gfxstream_vk_device.cpp
index cd4d693..9189b93 100644
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan/gfxstream_vk_device.cpp
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan/gfxstream_vk_device.cpp
@@ -88,6 +88,7 @@ static const char* const kGuestEmulatedInstanceExtensions[] = {
     VK_KHR_XCB_SURFACE_EXTENSION_NAME,
 #endif
     "VK_KHR_xcb_surface",
+    "VK_KHR_xlib_surface",
     "VK_EXT_headless_surface",
     VK_EXT_DEBUG_UTILS_EXTENSION_NAME,
 };
